Page 6 -an: -------- begin text --------
==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-an}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|ang|id=infinitival|:inh|gem-pro:*-aną|gem-pro:*-janą<id:causative>}}
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-aną}} and {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-janą|id=causative}}.

====Suffix====
{{ang-verb|cat=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{ng|marks the infinitive of most strong, class 1 weak, and preterite-present verbs (exceptions are verbs like {{m|ang|flēon|t=to flee}})}}
#: {{uxi|ang|[[singan|sing'''an''']]|t=to sing}}
#: {{uxi|ang|[[niman|nim'''an''']]|t=to take}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Verbs formed with this suffix from nominal suffixes that included [[back vowel]]s underwent [[i-umlaut]]. Thus, {{m|ang|dōm}} + ''-an'' is not *''dōman'', but {{m|ang|dēman}}, and {{m|ang|fōda}} + ''-an'' is not *''fōdan'', but {{m|ang|fēdan}}.

=====Conjugation=====
{{ang-conj|-an<w1/ge:0>}}
{{ang-conj-anglian|-an<w1/ge:0>}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desctree|enm|-en|id=infinitival}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymon|ang|id=ablative adverbial}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-anā}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-anē}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ang|-ane}}

====Suffix====
{{ang-adv}}

# {{ng|forms adverbs with ablative direction}}
#: {{uxi|ang|[[eastan|ēast'''an''']]|t=from the east}}
#: {{uxi|ang|[[westan|west'''an''']]|t=from the west}}

===Etymology 3===
{{etymon|ang|id=n-stem}}
{{inh+|ang|gmw-pro|*-an|id=n-stem}}, from a conflation of several {{inh|ang|gem-pro|-}} ''n-''stem suffixes: {{m|gem-pro|*-anų|pos=accusative singular}}, {{m|gem-pro|*-aniz|pos=genitive singular, nominative/vocative plural}} and {{m|gem-pro|*-anunz|pos=accusative plural}}.

Supplanted {{m+|gmw-pro|*-ōn}} during the prehistory of Old English except for in relic forms such as {{m|ang|ēastron}} and {{m|ang|foldu}}.

====Suffix====
{{ang-head|nounf|cat=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{n-g|marks the accusative, genitive, and dative singular and nominative and accusative plural of ''n''-stem nouns}}
#: {{uxi|ang|[[bera|ber'''an''']]|t=bear, bear's, bears}}

=====Declension=====
{{ang-decl-noun-n-m|-}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desctree|enm|-en|id=noun plural}}

===Etymology 4===

====Suffix====
{{ang-head|verbf|cat=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{alternative form of|ang|-on|pos=strong plural past indicative suffix}}

===Etymology 5===

====Suffix====
{{ang-head|adjf|cat=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{ng|forms the following inflections of weak adjectives:}}
## Masculine and feminine accusative, genitive, dative, and instrumental singular
## Neuter genitive, dative, and instrumental singular
## Masculine, feminine, and neuter nominative and accusative plural

===Etymology 6===
{{etymid|ang|-um}}

====Suffix====
{{ang-head|nounf|addlpos=adjf|cat=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{lb|ang|Late Old English}} {{alternative form of|ang|-um}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This form appears in late texts either due to reduction of the original {{m|ang|-um}} ending, influence from the ''n''-stem oblique singular and nominative/accusative plural {{m|ang|-an|id=n-stem}}, or most likely, a combination of both.

