==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-ast}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|ang|id=second-person singular|:inh|gmw-pro:*-ōs<ety:inh<gem-pro:*-ōsi<ety:inh<ine-pro:*-eh₂yési>>>>}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-ōs}} with paragogic ''-t'' added from when {{m|ang|þū}} follows (compare {{m+|ang-ang|-as}}), from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-ōsi}}, from {{inh|ang|ine-pro|*-eh₂yési}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ang|-as||Anglian}}

====Suffix====
{{h|ang|suf}}

# {{n-g|Used to form the second person singular present indicative of class II weak verbs}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|lufian|gloss1=to love|lufast|gloss2=you/thou love}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desctree|enm|-est|id=second-person singular}}

===Etymology 2===

====Suffix====
{{h|ang|suf}}

# {{alternative form of|ang|-ost}}

