==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ang|-bēre}}

===Etymology===
{{root|ang|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*bēriz||bearing, carrying}}. Akin to {{cog|ofs|-ber}}, {{cog|osx|-bāri}}, and {{cog|goh|-bāri}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|bǣre}}

===Suffix===
{{ang-adj|-bǣre}}

# {{ng|forms adjectives meaning “[[bearing]], [[having]]”}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|blostma<t:flower>|-bǣre|blostmbǣre<t:blooming>}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|feþer<t:feather>|-bǣre|feþerbǣre<t:feathered>}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|tungol<t:star>|-bǣre|tungolbǣre<t:starry>}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|wæstm<t:fruit>|-bǣre|wæstmbǣre<t:fruitful>}}
# {{ng|forms adjectives meaning “having the qualities of, characterized by”}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|and-<t:turned>|hēla<t:heel>|-bǣre|andelbǣre<t:inverted>}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|ātor<t:poison>|-bǣre|ātorbǣre<t:poisonous>}}
# {{ng|forms adjectives denoting likeness or similarity to}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|ċisel<t:gravel>|-bǣre|ċiselbǣre<t:gravelly>}}
# {{ng|forms adjectives meaning “producing”}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|cwealm<t:death>|-bǣre|cwealmbǣre<t:deadly>}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|slǣp<t:sleep>|-bǣre|slǣpbǣre<t:somniferous; putting to sleep>}}

====Declension====
{{ang-adecl|-bǣre}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|ang}}
