===Etymology===
{{unk|ang}}. There are no known cognates; {{w|Wilhelm Horn (Anglist)|Horn|lang=de}} posits derivation from {{der|ang|gem-pro||*hwō wegō}}, from {{af|gem-pro|*hwō|t1=how|*wegaz|alt2=*wegō|pos2=the instrumental of {{m|gem-pro|*wegaz}} "way"|lit=in what way, somehow|nocat=1}}.<ref>{{R:ang:AEW|-hwega, -u, -hwigu, -h(w)ugu||180}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book|year=1921|first=Wilhelm|last=Horn|authorlink=de:Wilhelm Horn (Anglist)|title=Sprachkörper und Sprachfunktion|series=Palaestra: Untersuchungen und Texte aus der Deutschen und Englischen Philologie|seriesvolume=135|publisher=Mayer & Müller|location=w:Berlin|oclc=12688244|page=82|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/HornSprachkorper/page/n97}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|hwugu}}

===Suffix===
{{h|ang|suf}} {{lb|ang|indeclinable}}

# [[some]]- ''(forms indefinite pronouns and adverbs from interrogatives)''
#: {{suffixusex|ang|hwǣr|t1=where|hwǣrhwugu|t2=somewhere}}
#: {{suffixusex|ang|hwæt|t1=what|hwæthwugu|t2=something}}

====Usage notes====
* Pronouns appended to ''-hwugu'' are still inflected: ''Sprec wiþ mē be <u>hwām</u>hwugu þā hwīle þe iċ sēoðe'' (“Talk to me about something while I'm cooking”).

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|ang|ā-||any-}}
* {{l|ang|ǣġ-||every-}}

