* The variant form ''-eġ'' (or ''-eg'') often occurs specifically when followed by suffixes containing back vowels. Ringe and Taylor (2014) suggest that prehistoric ''*-ag'' failed to fully raise to ''-iġ'' in this environment, with the variant reflecting a preserved transitional form<ref>{{R:ang:DOE|page=335}}</ref>.

