==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|ang|stōw||place}}, from {{der|ang|gem-pro|*stōō||place}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*steh₂w-||to set, place}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*steh₂-||to stand}}. Akin to {{cog|non|-stó||place of}}, {{cog|ofs|stō||place}}, {{cog|got|𐍃𐍄𐍉𐌾𐌰𐌽||to judge, place}}. Compare the similar usage in forming toponyms in the cognate {{cog|iir}} suffix {{m|en|-stan}}. See also {{m|en|stow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-stṑw}}

===Suffix===
{{h|ang|suf|head=-stōw|g=f}}

