==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ang|-waras|-waran|-waru}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-wari}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*warjaz|t=dwellers of}}. Cognate with {{cog|goh|-āri|t=inhabitants of}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-wàre}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ang|suffix|g=m-p}}

# {{lb|ang|used in the singular}} suffix denoting inhabitants or residents of a place
#: {{uxi|ang|eall sēo buruh'''waru'''|the people of a city, the entire citizenry}}
# {{lb|ang|used in the plural}} suffix denoting inhabitants or residents of a place
#: {{uxi|ang|[[burgwaras|burg'''waras''']]|residents of a burg, burghers, citizens}}
#: {{uxi|ang|[[Lundenwaran|Lundun'''waran''']]|Londoners}}
#: {{uxi|ang|[[Rōmware|Rōm'''ware''']]|residents of Rome; Romans}}

