{{etymon|ang|:inh|gem-pro:*wardaz<id:turn>}}
From {{der|ang|gem-pro|*wardaz|t=turned toward, in the direction of, facing}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*wert-|t=to turn, wind}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*wer-|t=to turn, bend}}.

Akin to {{cog|ofs|-ward}}, {{cog|osx|-ward}}, {{cog|non|verðr}}, {{cog|de|-wärts}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|weorþan|t=to turn (into), become}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-wèard}}

===Suffix===
{{h|ang|suf}}

# {{n-g|Forming adjectives and nouns from adjectives or prepositions, with the sense of "in the direction of, toward".}}
#: {{uxi|ang|[[ēasteweard|ēaste'''weard''']]|eastward}}, {{uxi|ang|[[tōweard|tō'''weard''']]|future|q=adjective and noun}}
# {{n-g|Forming adverbs from adjectives or prepositions, with the sense of "in the direction of, toward".}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ang|-weardes}}
{{suffixsee|ang}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|enm|-warde|-ward}}
