Page 237 -wyrde: -------- begin text --------
==Old English==

===Etymology===
Compound words from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*wurdiją}}. More at {{l|ang|word}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-wyrde}}

===Suffix===
{{ang-adj|-wyrde}}

# {{n-g|Forming adjectives and nouns from adjectives, with the sense of "a kind of speech".}}
#: {{ux|ang|Wes ðū ðīnum yldrum ārfæst symle, '''fæġerwyrde'''|Be thou ever honourable to thine elders, '''fair in word'''}}
#: {{ux|ang|þæt gē ne bēon tō '''biterwyrde''', ne bealufulle on mōde|That ye be not '''bitter in speech''', nor baleful in spirit}}

====Derived terms====
{{col|ang
|bealdwyrde<t:bold in speech>
|biterwyrde<t:bitter in speech>
|fæġerwyrde<t:fair in speech>
|felawyrde<t:many-worded, talkative>
|hōcorwyrde<t:scornful, derisive>
|hrædwyrde<t:hasty in speech>
|līþwyrde<t:gentle in speech>
|snotorwyrde<t:prudent in speech>
|stuntwyrde<t:foolish in speech>
|swǣswyrde<t:pleasant in speech>
|wærwyrde<t:wary, cautious in speech>
|wīswyrde<t:wise in speech>
}}

===Suffix===
{{ang-noun||n}}

# {{n-g|Forming nouns from nouns or adjectives, with the sense of "a kind of speech".}}
#: {{ux|ang|Hētan him ðæt '''andwyrde''' secgan|They ordered him to give that '''answer'''}}
#: {{ux|ang|Ðæt ic mǣge sum rust on weg adrīfan of mīnre tungan, ðæt ic mǣge becuman to brǣddran '''gewyrde'''|That I may drive away some rust from my tongue, so that I may attain more broader '''verbosity'''}}

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-n|-wyrd|nomsg=-wyrde}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ang|andwyrde||answer}}
* {{l|ang|ġewyrde||speech, conversation, verbosity}}
* {{l|ang|bīwyrde||byword, proverb}}
* {{l|ang|fracoþwyrde||insult, abusive language}}
